<br/>
Apple is not identified in the documents; its involvement is known about because of <em>Bloomberg</em>'s report. Labels also refer to Hyundai HT Global's factory in Vietnam. <br/>
<br/>
The three devices are part of a broader <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/2026/10/06/lg-apple-smart-home-products/">seven-product lineup</a> that reportedly also includes a wired video doorbell, indoor security camera, outdoor security camera, and floodlight camera. LG will sell the accessories under its own brand, with Apple reportedly helping to shape their designs, features, and engineering. The arrangement would allow Apple to easily expand its home ecosystem while LG handles production and support.<br/>
<br/>
Apple and LG have collaborated before, including on <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/2016/10/27/apple-4k-5k-lg-displays-new-macbook-pro/">UltraFine 4K and 5K displays</a> designed for Macs. LG also expanded its smart home business in 2024 by acquiring an 80% stake in Athom, the company behind the Homey smart home platform.<br/>
<br/>
Apple is reportedly preparing an aggressive expansion into the smart home market, with a <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/2026/09/30/apple-home-products-coming-on-october-13/">new home hub, Apple TV 4K, and HomePod mini</a> expected on October 13. Its longer-term plans also include a <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/guide/apple-robot/">higher-end home hub</a> with a display mounted on a robotic arm. Apple is separately developing its own AI-powered <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/2026/10/07/apple-home-security-camera-still-coming-next-year/">home security camera and sensor</a>, which remains distinct from LG's accessories and is still expected in 2027.<div class="linkback">Tags: <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/guide/apple-home/">Apple Home</a>, <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/guide/homekit/">HomeKit</a>, <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/guide/lg/">LG</a>, <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/guide/pdfu/">pdfu</a></div><br/>This article, &quot;<a href="https://www.macrumors.com/2026/10/07/first-look-at-lg-apple-smart-home-products/">First Look at LG&#039;s Smart Home Products Made With Apple</a>&quot; first appeared on <a href="https://www.macrumors.com">MacRumors.com</a><br/><br/><a href="https://forums.macrumors.com/threads/first-look-at-lgs-smart-home-products-made-with-apple.2491257/">Discuss this article</a> in our forums<br/><br/>